  <ctml:notes>Sofia Cup 2026 - Balkan Rapid Championship, Sofia (Grand Hotel Sofia), 2026-08-29: a 9-round individual Swiss, rapid time control 600+5, organized by Chess Club "Maritza-Iztok" (Radnevo) and FIDE-rated for rapid. Part of Sofia Cup 2026, which ran two SEPARATE championships (this Rapid and the Blitz); they have different round counts and fields, so each is its own file. Winner: Mamedov, Rauf (7.5/9). 185 players, 806 games and 8 full-point byes (byes recorded as nonGame kind=bye). The complete field, all results, byes, and per-move clocks come from the chess.com PGN; movetext exists only for the broadcast (top ~20) boards, so lower boards are recorded result-only (626 of 806). ECO is classified from movetext by longest UCI-prefix match (no ECO in the export). Official final standings (top 50, transcribed) give placement, seed, and federation for the top 50; every player's score is recomputed from the games plus byes and REPRODUCES the official points for all top 50 exactly (placements below 50 are not asserted - only the top 50 were available). Rating snapshots are the FIDE rapid ratings carried by the chess.com PGN (they match the official standings' rating column). Identity is by FIDE id (two blitz players lacking one are identified by name). Source note: an independent broadcast PGN (Lichess/TWIC, top boards only) disagreed with chess.com on the winner of 8 rapid games (identical moves, resignation/time endings); chess.com's results reproduce the official points exactly, so chess.com is authoritative and those broadcast result tags are errors. Uses the CTML 2.1 model (participant/placement/seed; nonGame byes).</ctml:notes>
  <ctml:source kind="chess.com-pgn">
    <ctml:uri>file:///D:/dev/pgn/sofia-cup-2026-balkan-rapid-and-blitz-championships-rapid.pgn</ctml:uri>
    <ctml:note>Complete field, all results, byes, and per-move clocks (broadcast boards). 814 records. SHA-256 ce9491db91c3e123e737385d95d2f47d18e6303b57fcc4849c412c3f24730065.</ctml:note>
  </ctml:source>
